# ROUND7 — oodar 8D substrate audit (v3.4.2)
File: oodar/audit/round7.oot

Scope: /home/jeryd/Projects/openOODA/oodar only. Tag v3.4.2, HEAD 630d943.
Method: 8D Red Team (practices/8d-red-team.oot). Negative trust.
Empirical: make lint; 10 challenger tests; dudect; contract double-run.

Verdict: user-space oo_cap_require_* on named mutators is fail-closed
for cap=0 (56/56, two fresh processes). That is not a hermetic jail.
Zero ambient authority does not hold. Do not claim fail-closed kernel
mediation until the CRITICAL items below are closed.

# Empirical surface (green is not proof)

- lint-anchors, lint-file-size, lint-cap-table: PASS
- contract 56/56 cap=0: PASS, double-run identical
- cap_escape, cap_threat, attenuate_v2, differential_cap: PASS
- pathcap, proc_mem_leak, sandbox_containment, actor_race: PASS
- fuzz_smoke 200 iters: PASS
- dudect: HMAC |t|=924 < 4500; cg_sign self-vs-self |t|=22;
  branchy |t|=45138 >= 4500. HMAC probe is real. cg_sign probe is vacuous.
- api_surface: oodar.c includes = UMBRELLA_SRCS = VERSION 95. Holds.
- C line cap: only mldsa_internal.c (627) and mlkem_internal.c (472)
  over 256. Both are documented exceptions. mlkem claim of 460 is stale.

# CRITICAL (verified on disk)

1. oo_slist_new applies seccomp with no cap.
   core/list/list.c:99-102 calls oo_sandbox_apply().
   sandbox_config.c:204-223 installs BPF. Default g_sand_net=0 and
   g_sand_proc=0 so first string-list alloc denies socket and fork.
   Status backend is set to LINUX_LANDLOCK_SECCOMP with no Landlock.
   Fix: delete the call. Require SysCap on apply. Never stamp Landlock
   on a seccomp-only path.

2. Seccomp install failure still reports enforced.
   sandbox_config.c:79-87. fail_closed_on_kernel_miss defaults to 0.
   Filter failure is swallowed. Return is still
   OK_LINUX_LANDLOCK_SECCOMP_ENFORCED. Fix: always fail closed.
   Do not advertise seccomp unless the filter is installed.

3. Public process spawn with no cap.
   oodar.h:69 ffi_verify_signature. ffi_sec.c:54-91 forks and
   execlp("minisign"). oo_dlopen calls it after FfiCap, but the
   symbol is on the public ABI without a cap argument.
   Same class: oo_process_policy_getenv (sys_env.c:14-19) is getenv
   without EnvCap; oo_child_filter_env mutates environ with no cap.
   Fix: unexport or require FfiCap/EnvCap on every OS-touching symbol.

4. HMAC heap overflow on negative OoStr.len.
   sec/crypto/symmetric/hmac.c:22-26. size_t(msg.len) wraps, then
   memcpy of 64 ipad bytes overruns malloc. Fix: reject len < 0
   before any size_t cast.

# HIGH

5. Rule 2 is not bound to the parent seal.
   cap_attenuate_hmac.c:51-64 HMAC(parent_hmac, child_rights) only.
   Caller-supplied parent_rights is not in the MAC. v1 API has no
   subset check and stays public. Fix: MAC parent_rights; remove v1.

6. OoPathCap is prefix-memcmp and unwired.
   cap_attenuate_path.c:185-188. /tmp matches /tmpfoo. Re-attenuation
   uses the raw parent token so prefixes can widen. oo_read_file never
   calls oo_path_cap_check. Fix: directory-boundary check; wire FS ops
   or delete the API.

7. TimeCap/RandCap still use 56-bit entropy plus a type band.
   cap_time.c:41-52. Violates SECURITY_MODEL Rule 1 (no type bits).
   Fix: same make_cap_tok as caps.c.

8. atexit zeroize misses split stores.
   caps.c:64-89 wipes 22 tokens plus HMAC key. Does not wipe
   g_tok_alloc, g_tok_ffi, g_tok_time, g_tok_rand. SIGKILL residual
   remains. Fix: one zeroize that covers every store.

9. pq_aead_open drops plaintext and returns "verified".
   pq_aead_open.c:116-128. Decrypt is not a decrypt.

10. UDP dotted IPv4 bypasses the loopback claim.
    netfloor_udp.c:63-69. inet_aton success sends to any IPv4.
    TCP connect (netfloor_tcp.c) uses unrestricted getaddrinfo
    despite a loopback-only comment.

11. write_int/read_int UAF vs oo_free.
    alloc.c:149-168 recovers the header by pointer arithmetic
    without the alloc-table mutex. Concurrent free is UAF.

12. Actor/channel send vs destroy TOCTOU.
    live is read without the slot mutex; destroy destroys the mutex.
    actor_race only covers otp_supervise.

13. Vacuous tests.
    dudect cg_sign is self-vs-self. proc_mem_leak Phase B allowlists
    only tmpdir so /proc/self/mem deny cannot fail. cap_threat treats
    raw socket success as INFO. contract omits oo_sandbox_apply,
    oo_write_file, oo_now_ms, oo_random, oo_write_int, oo_free.
    lint-cap-table diffs generator output against itself; require
    names oo_cap_require_fs_write do not match C symbols.

14. Docs and tables disagree with caps.h.
    SECURITY_MODEL.oot still says 25 tokens and 0x800 reserved.
    METRICS is 0x800. Bind is required on tcp_bind/bind_udp but
    ANCHOR.oo still calls Bind future-state. TESTING.oot still
    says 5 challenger tests (disk has 10). COMPILER_READ has no
    consumer; host.c uses FfiCap. cap_table.json _version 3.1.1.

# MEDIUM

15. Landlock probe_backend is compile-time #ifdef, not ABI.
16. g_ll_applied is a user-space bool; oo_landlock_mark_applied
    is a global ELF symbol with no cap.
17. FS read uses realpath then fopen (symlink TOCTOU). Write uses
    openat+O_NOFOLLOW.
18. Landlock read bits include EXECUTE.
19. oo_random returns -1 on getentropy failure (not abort).
20. oo_meta_epoch sets -1 on getentropy failure (not abort).
21. Arena checkpoint is a global long-long stack, not arena restore.
22. Weak-ref TOCTOU UAF (epoch unused).
23. AES-GCM uses secret-indexed S-boxes; dudect does not probe AEAD.
24. Makefile 337 lines (claimed 331). Two .py files drive CI lint.
    repro_build.sh is an extra host script. CHANGES.md extra .md.
25. examples/ is empty (RFC-0005 placeholder).
26. 25 nested ANCHOR.oo files omit Setup.

# Residuals still true (prior audits)

- 64-bit tokens live in the same address space as /proc/self/mem.
- atexit does not run on SIGKILL.
- Seccomp is a small allow-default denylist, not the cap table.
- No C RASP rollback. oo_rollback is not arena restore.

# Closed this tree (do not re-litigate as live)

- LCG fallbacks on cap/HMAC-key derivation: abort on getentropy fail.
- Public mutator cap=0 require: 56/56 fail-closed.
- otp_supervise unlocked double-restart: actor_race 8 threads, 1 success.
- Umbrella file count matches VERSION api_surface=95.

# Next (priority order)

1. Remove oo_sandbox_apply from oo_slist_new. Cap-gate apply.
2. Fail closed when seccomp install fails. Stop the lying OK string.
3. Unexport or cap-gate ffi_verify_signature and policy getenv.
4. Reject negative HMAC lengths.
5. Bind Rule 2 rights into the HMAC. Wire or delete OoPathCap.
6. Sync SECURITY_MODEL, CAPABILITIES_TABLE, TESTING, ANCHORs to v3.4.2.
7. Add hostile tests that fail on items 1-6 before claiming complete.
